- * - `status`: `1` on success, `0` if the time step scaling factor is lower
- *   than 0.99 at some points, `-1` if the computations failed at some
- *   points, `-2` for invalid arguments, `-3` for a runtime error of the
- *   backend;
- * - `first_failure_index`: index of the first point where the computations
- *   failed, or the maximal value of the type if no point failed.
+ * - `1`: the integration succeeded at all points;
+ * - `0`: the integration succeeded at all points, but the time step scaling
+ *   factor is lower than 0.99 at some points;
+ * - `-1`: the integration failed at some points;
+ * - `-2`: invalid arguments, nothing was computed;
+ * - `-3`: runtime error of the backend (allocation, kernel launch, etc.).
+ *
+ * `MGIS` reports the statuses `-2` and `-3` by exceptions.
  */
 typedef struct mgis_bv_BatchOutputStatus {
+  //! \brief status
   int status;
+  //! \brief number of points where the integration failed
   mgis_size_type number_of_failures;
+  /*!
